# AWS vs Azure Cost Comparison

## Compute Costs

AWS and Azure provide similar virtual machine configurations suitable for hosting a small web application.

AWS uses EC2 instances while Azure uses Virtual Machines.

## Storage Costs

AWS uses Amazon S3.

Azure uses Azure Storage Accounts.

Both provide scalable object storage suitable for application files and backups.

## Networking

Both providers charge for outbound internet traffic.

Data transferred between Availability Zones also incurs charges depending on the region.

## Discount Comparison

AWS

- Savings Plans
- Reserved Instances
- Spot Instances

Azure

- Reserved VM Instances
- Azure Hybrid Benefit
- Spot Virtual Machines

## Cost Effectiveness

For Linux workloads, AWS is often a strong choice due to competitive compute pricing.

For Windows workloads, Azure becomes more attractive when Azure Hybrid Benefit is used because existing Windows Server licenses reduce licensing costs.

## Cost Optimization Strategies

1. Use Reserved Instances or Savings Plans for long-term workloads.
2. Enable auto-scaling and regularly review resource usage to avoid paying for idle resources.
